  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The distance between object A and object B is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x\"></span> and the gravitational force acting between the objects is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F\"></span>. The mass of object A is increased by <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"50\"></span> percent and the mass of object B is decreased by <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"50\"></span> percent. What should be the distance between the objects in order for the gravitational force to triple?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{x}{2}\"></span> </li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{2}}\"></span> </li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{x}{3}\"></span> </li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
